      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.1,
      "end_seconds": 276.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like primary dysmenorrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.41,
      "end_seconds": 324.42,
      "duration_seconds": 32.01,
      "text": "You'll be taking naproxen, 250 milligrams, three times a day with food, during periods. That should help with period pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Heat, gentle exercise, and and start the tablet at the first sign of pain. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's plan a check in three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.29,
      "end_seconds": 329.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
